ance","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%27s_Bay_Company","c":3},{"y":1695,"t":"gain","x":"1695: the company recovers York Factory ('the company recovered it the next year').","cp":"new-france","cpn":"New France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%27s_Bay_Company","c":3},{"y":1697,"t":"loss","x":"1697: d'Iberville again takes York Factory.","m":9,"cp":"new-france","cpn":"New France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%27s_Bay_Company","c":3},{"y":1713,"t":"gain","x":"1713: Hudson Bay returns to Britain.","m":4,"cp":"new-france","cpn":"New France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Utrecht","c":3},{"y":1713,"t":"contest_end","x":"1713: the Hudson Bay fighting ends with the Treaty of Utrecht (11 April 1713).","m":4,"cp":"new-france","cpn":"New France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Utrecht","c":3},{"y":1818,"t":"loss","x":"1818: the 49th parallel becomes the southern border.","m":10,"cp":"united-states-of-america","cpn":"United States of America","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convention_of_1818","c":2},{"y":1821,"t":"gain","x":"1821: the company's monopoly reaches the Pacific.","m":12,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupert%27s_Land","c":2},{"y":1862,"t":"loss","x":"1862: the Stickeen Territory is split off.","m":7,"cp":"Stickeen Territory","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stikine_Territory","c":3},{"y":1863,"t":"loss","x":"1863: the north-east goes to British Columbia.","cp":"colony-of-british-columbia","cpn":"Colony of British Columbia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colony_of_British_Columbia_(1858%E2%80%931866)","c":2},{"y":1863,"t":"gain","x":"1863: the land north of the 60th parallel returns.","m":7,"cp":"Stickeen Territory","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stikine_Territory","c":3},{"y":1870,"t":"loss","x":"1870: Rupert's Land passes to Canada.","m":7,"cp":"canada","cpn":"Canada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupert%27s_Land","c":3},{"y":1870,"t":"dissolve","x":"1870: Rupert's Land is disestablished on 15 July 1870; the Red River provisional government negotiated with the new Canadian government that year (the 'Red River Rebellion').","m":7,"cp":"canada","cpn":"Canada","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupert%27s_Land","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Hudson Bay raids of the Anglo-French rivalry","from":1686,"to":1713,"outcome":"France took the James Bay posts in 1686 and York Factory in 1694 and 1697 (the company recovered it in 1695) and kept all the outposts except Fort Albany until the Treaty of Utrecht returned the bay to Britain in 1713.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%27s_Bay_Company"}],"certainty":[{"from":1670,"to":1817,"level":"soft","note":"A chartered claim to a drainage basin: no survey, only coastal posts; the French posts of 1686-1713 on James Bay and Hudson Bay are the exception in detail only."},{"from":1818,"to":1870,"level":"soft","note":"The southern border is sharp along the 49th parallel from the Convention of 1818 (Lake of the Woods to the Rocky Mountains); the boundaries with the North-Western Territory, with Russian America and with Labrador stay approximate."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stikine_Territory","title":"Stikine Territory"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colony_of_British_Columbia_(1858%E2%80%931866)","title":"Colony of British Columbia (1858-1866)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rupert%27s_Land","title":"Rupert's Land"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hudson%27s_Bay_Company","title":"Hudson's Bay Company"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convention_of_1818","title":"Convention of 1818"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North-Western_Territory","title":"North-Western Territory"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Utrecht","title":"Treaty of Utrecht"}]}